  "station_1_title": "Matai'an Wetland Ecological Park Overview",
  "station_1_intro": "Step into Hualien's purest natural paradise, experiencing the raw charm of interlocking spring wetlands and indigenous Amis culture.",
  "station_1_audio_open": "Welcome to Matai'an Wetland! Let's explore Hualien's purest natural paradise together.",
  "station_1_audio_desc": "Before you lies a vast wetland where waterways crisscross and wild grasses gently sway, creating a tranquil and serene atmosphere. As you stroll down the trail, you can spot schools of fish darting by and elegant waterbirds foraging gracefully.",
  "station_1_audio_story": "Matai'an Wetland serves as a vital traditional living ground for the Amis people and is a rare inland wetland fed by continuous natural springs in Taiwan. Local people have fostered deep wisdom in coexisting with nature, allowing this land to nourish a rich ecosystem of diverse flora and fauna.",
  "station_1_audio_interact": "Why not slow your pace, look closely at the crystal-clear water surfaces and lush bushes, and see how many different species you can spot?",
  "station_1_audio_end": "Feel the most harmonious distance between humanity and nature within this raw, tranquil wetland. Welcome, and let your exploration begin.",
  
  "station_2_title": "Palakaw Ecological Wisdom",
  "station_2_intro": "A hand-crafted three-layer 'eco-mansion' tailored beautifully for fish and shrimp, embodying a sustainable philosophy of taking only what you need.",
  "station_2_audio_open": "Hey there! Have you ever heard a magical story about catching fish without hooks, simply by building them a custom house?",
  "station_2_audio_desc": "Take a look at the clear pool right in front of you. What looks like scattered timber logs and hollow bamboo segments is actually a 'three-story luxury apartment' crafted meticulously by the Amis for aquatic life.",
  "station_2_audio_story": "This unique architectural approach is called 'Palakaw'. The bottom layer of large hollow bamboo acts as cozy bedrooms for eels and swamp eels; the middle layer of dense tree branches provides a safe haven and playground for shrimp and crabs away from predators; and the top layer of grasses and palm leaves serves as a shaded nursery for small fry. Upholding the spirit of 'take only what you need, never over-harvest', the Amis build them homes first and harvest mature fish selectively later.",
  "station_2_audio_interact": "Now, you can step closer to the water's edge, or roll up your pants to dip your feet into this refreshing spring stream. Feel the structure of the fish traps, and try to find if there are any tiny shrimp hiding in the bamboo crevices!",
  "station_2_audio_end": "This eco-friendly coexistence system represents a millennium-old ancestral philosophy of life, inspiring deep respect for the wisdom of the earth.",
  
  "station_3_title": "Visitor Center & Xinlv Farm Entrance",
  "station_3_intro": "Starting from the eye-catching iconic giant frog landmark, step into a welcoming gateway blending local farm-to-table cuisine and indigenous culture.",
  "station_3_audio_open": "Welcome to the Matai'an Leisure Agricultural Area! Let's kick off a natural journey in sync with the heartbeat of the wetland.",
  "station_3_audio_desc": "Right at this entrance, you will spot an incredibly eye-catching giant frog statue, which serves as a major landmark for navigating the park. Right next to it is Xinlv Farm, a vibrant gathering spot filled with warm local stories and hospitality.",
  "station_3_audio_story": "This area is the ideal starting point for cyclists and independent travelers entering the wetland. The venue showcases how the Amis have structured their lives according to the natural rhythms of the seasons for generations, beautifully weaving sustainable eco-farming and indigenous heritage together.",
  "station_3_audio_interact": "Don't miss taking a fun photo with this cute giant frog, and imagine yourself transforming into a little frog jumping through the marshes as you start this eco-adventure!",
  "station_3_audio_end": "Keep this lively entrance fresh in your mind as you begin the most authentic and complete exploration of Matai'an.",
  
  "station_4_title": "Amis Traditional Stone Hotpot Experience",
  "station_4_intro": "Using glowing red-hot stones and fresh green bamboo tubes, witness an astonishing, zero-waste culinary magic show.",
  "station_4_audio_open": "Did you know that without using gas stoves or modern cookware, you can boil a mouth-watering, fresh fish soup using nothing but raw stones?",
  "station_4_audio_desc": "Right here, you can see fresh green bamboo segments filled with pure spring water, wild greens, fish, and shrimp. Beside them, glowing red-hot serpentine stones are being heated in a crackling bonfire, filling the air with woodsmoke and subtle bamboo aromas.",
  "station_4_audio_story": "This is the ancestral wisdom of the Amis 'stone-cooking method'. The host drops glowing red-hot stones directly into the liquid-filled bamboo tube, instantly creating a dramatic sizzling sound and sending up billows of aromatic steam. The extreme heat boils the soup in seconds, locking in the natural sweetness of the ingredients. To respect the environment, this dining ritual promotes a zero-waste 'slow food culture'—no paper napkins are provided; instead, you wash your hands directly in the pure stream water.",
  "station_4_audio_interact": "Listen closely to the marvelous symphony of hot stones colliding with cold spring water, and breathe in that rich, natural aroma. Isn't your mouth watering already?",
  "station_4_audio_end": "This is far more than a delicious local feast; it's a touching experience of resourcefulness and living in perfect harmony with nature.",
  
  "station_5_title": "Pigeon Pea (Fata'an) and the Origin of the Place Name",
  "station_5_intro": "Meet the soul plant that gave this entire wetland its name—the pigeon pea, symbolizing resilient vitality and indigenous energy.",
  "station_5_audio_open": "Hello friends! Looking at all the rich greenery around us, do you know which plant gave this historic land its name?",
  "station_5_audio_desc": "Take a look around you. You can see rows of shrubs laden with bean pods swaying gently in the breeze. That is the precious 'pigeon pea', treasured dearly by the Amis people.",
  "station_5_audio_story": "The name 'Matai'an' actually originates from the Amis word 'Fata'an', which translates directly to 'pigeon pea'. Historically, this land was covered with wild pigeon peas. They served as a vital traditional staple food and source of energy for the tribe—fostering strength and health—and became a lasting symbol of resilience for this homeland.",
  "station_5_audio_interact": "Feel free to step closer to examine the unique leaves and hanging pods, touch its sturdy branches, and guess what kind of hearty traditional soup the Amis love to brew with it?",
  "station_5_audio_end": "Remember this humble little pigeon pea, for it represents the deepest, most enduring cultural roots anchoring the history of Matai'an.",
  
  "station_6_title": "Fuden River & Ecological Wooden Walkway",
  "station_6_intro": "Stroll along the elevated, winding boardwalk overlooking the pristine Fuden River, discovering a gentle pact between humans and nature.",
  "station_6_audio_open": "The path beneath your feet right now is much more than just a wooden walkway—it is a elevated gateway into the living heartbeat of the wetland.",
  "station_6_audio_desc": "This winding boardwalk is built elevated above the crystal-clear Fuden River. Thick patches of water plants sway gracefully with the current below, surrounded by vibrant greenery and the soothing melody of flowing water.",
  "station_6_audio_story": "The Fuden River is the life-giving artery of Matai'an. Before this protective boardwalk was constructed, visitors walking randomly would damage the fragile marsh mud and plants. Today, this elevated path serves as a 'gentle pact', allowing us to admire nature up close without disturbing the homes of these precious small creatures.",
  "station_6_audio_interact": "Please slow your steps or take a brief pause to gaze down into the transparent spring water. See if you can spot little fish weaving through the water grass, or close your eyes to take a deep breath of the crisp, fresh air.",
  "station_6_audio_end": "When you leave, may you carry away not just photos in your album, but the serene inner peace of having coexisted beautifully with this earth.",
  
  "station_7_title": "Water Willow Area & Night Firefly Tour",
  "station_7_intro": "Step into a serene swamp realm of water willows, searching for blinking green lights in the summer night—nature's signature report card of health.",
  "station_7_audio_open": "Welcome, everyone! Are you ready to venture with us into this enchanting 'forest of lights' that reveals itself only at night?",
  "station_7_audio_desc": "We are currently standing in the Water Willow Area, surrounded by a majestic grove of water willows thriving naturally in the marshes. As darkness falls completely, magical points of blinking green light will slowly illuminate the air all around you.",
  "station_7_audio_story": "Water willows are remarkably adapted to aquatic soils and play an important role in purifying water quality. This area is a thriving sanctuary for fireflies, which are highly sensitive bioindicators—they can only survive in environments with immaculate water quality and zero light pollution. Their twinkling lives are actively declaring to us: This land is completely healthy!",
  "station_7_audio_interact": "Now, let's turn off our bright flashlights and smartphones, slow down our footsteps, and lower our voices. Let your eyes adjust to the darkness and count how many blinking fireflies you can discover around you.",
  "station_7_audio_end": "Keep the memory of tonight's delicate lights and the reflections of the water willows close to your heart, for this nocturnal display is nature's highest medal of environmental health awarded to Matai'an."
}